        "Restore perfusion with prescribed isotonic fluids, assess potassium and renal status, and monitor. Current adult consensus: if K⁺ is below 3.5 mmol/L, replace it and delay insulin until above 3.5. When glucose falls below 250 mg/dL, dextrose can allow insulin to continue until ketoacidosis resolves. Glucose improvement alone does not prove resolution."
